---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
layout: false
---
{#- /sitemap.xml — referenced from /robots.txt.

   collections.all is exactly the right set without any filtering here, and that is
   not an accident: every page that must not be indexed already carries
   `eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true` — /analytics/, /curation/, /redirect.html,
   and the species-slug redirect stubs. If a new unlisted page is ever added without
   that flag it will appear here, which is what sitemap.test.ts guards.

   No <lastmod>: the site is rebuilt nightly from CSVs, so a build timestamp would
   tell crawlers every one of the ~1,300 pages changed every day, which is both false
   and a reason for them to stop trusting the field. Omitting it is better than
   filling it with noise.
-#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for item in collections.all %}
  <url><loc>{{ item.url | url | absoluteUrl }}</loc></url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
